# uni-lab.local.hosts — the authoritative uni-lab.local NAME MAP (dnsmasq addn-hosts).
# THE ONE declared source of truth for fleet names. Format: <IP> <fqdn> [aliases].
# dnsmasq serves an A record per line and auto-generates the matching PTR (reverse) record.
# Multi-homed names carry several lines; `localise-queries` in dnsmasq.uni.conf returns the
# A record on the SAME subnet the query arrived on, so one clean name is plane-correct:
#   a LAN querier gets 10.190.245.x · a wg querier gets 10.13.13.x · a Tailscale querier gets 100.x.
# NV = backend not verified live (box/port down in survey); the NAME is correct — it must not be
# treated as "up" until its live probe passes (see viewer/infra.cjs). Lines commented with
# "# NV-HOLD" are withheld until a gate proves them (uncomment after the named gate).
#
# Corresponds 1:1 to viewer/infra_registry.json ON NAMES. It no longer mirrors the chip's ADDRESS, and
# must not: as of 2026-07-16 the registry declares NO LAN address for the chip (see its
# _lan_dynamic_law). The chip's LAN address is a DHCP lease on a disposable uplink, so THIS FILE — the
# zone uni-dns serves — is its single source of truth. Studio consumers resolve the name through
# viewer/host_resolve.cjs and follow whatever this file says; gate: node viewer/verify_host_tracking.cjs.
#
# WHY THE OLD "keep the two in sync" INSTRUCTION FAILED (2026-07-16): the lease moved .122 -> .121 and
# this file, the NRPT rule and infra.cjs's bootstrap literals were all updated — infra_registry.json was
# not. Nothing enforced the sync, so the Door's hrefs, the HUD's links, Gaia's colony collectors, the
# glass badge ssh pusher and the litigation-hold mind capture all addressed a dead host while the colony
# was demonstrably LIVE. The sync requirement is gone because the duplicate declaration is gone.
#
# ON THE NEXT LEASE MOVE, exactly two places need the new address (not ~15): the chip lines below, and
# THINKER's NRPT rule (viewer/apply_nrpt.ps1). Automating that is the reconciliation beacon — P1 of
# docs/handoffs/ADAPTIVE_SELF_NETWORK_HANDOFF_2026-07-15.md. Until it lands this is a hand edit.
# Receipt: docs/receipts/chip_address_tracking_2026-07-16.md
#
# APPLYING AN EDIT TO THIS ZONE (learned live 2026-08-01, at the cost of a few seconds of DNS):
#   uni-dns is a dnsmasq CONTAINER that FILE-bind-mounts this file. Editing the file is not enough — the
#   running dnsmasq must be told to re-read, and the ONLY correct way is:
#         systemctl restart uni-dns.service
#   Two tempting shortcuts are BOTH wrong and were both proven wrong on 2026-08-01:
#   * A SIGHUP (`podman kill --signal HUP uni-dns`) re-reads a STALE inode. An atomic writer swaps the
#     file's inode on save, but the file bind-mount is pinned to the OLD inode, so dnsmasq faithfully
#     re-reads the pre-edit text (it logged "90 names" when the file already held 96).
#   * `podman restart uni-dns` REMOVES the container — the Quadlet runs it with --rm — and does not bring
#     it back, dropping DNS *and* DHCP on the chip. `systemctl restart uni-dns.service` recreates it from
#     the Quadlet unit, which re-resolves the bind-mount to the current inode. Confirm with:
#         podman logs uni-dns  (expect: "read /etc/uni/dns/uni-lab.local.hosts - <N> names")

# ── SERVICES (uni-lab / "the chip", L1 — colony + ERP + DNS) ────────────────────────────────
10.190.245.121   dns.uni-lab.local
10.13.13.1       dns.uni-lab.local
100.100.188.48   dns.uni-lab.local

10.89.1.40       mc.uni-lab.local
# NV-HOLD (gate: prove a host port-forward of :25565): a LAN A record for mc.uni-lab.local.
# Withheld, and verified still withheld 2026-07-16: :25565 and :25575 time out from THINKER because
# mc-server binds COLNET (10.89.1.40) only — unroutable from the studio. This is why Gaia's
# colony.mc.port.25565 / colony.rcon.port.25575 read DOWN against a healthy, LIVE colony: structural,
# NOT address drift. Do not "fix" it by adding an address here — uncomment only when the port-forward
# gate passes, and write the chip's CURRENT lease address (see the header: this file is its one source).

10.190.245.121   colony.uni-lab.local
10.190.245.121   colonycam.uni-lab.local
